# Brief template

Fill this in yourself after `watch.py` produces the raw diff. Keep it short —
one screen. The script gives you facts; you provide judgment.

---

## Competitor feature brief — {period}

### TL;DR
{Two or three sentences: what actually happened, and the single thing that matters most to us.}

### {Competitor A}

**Shipped:** {cluster the raw changes into 1–3 themes, not a changelog dump}
**So what:** {why it matters to our product / roadmap / positioning}
**Source:** {link the exact release/changelog item}

### {Competitor B}
...

### Watchlist (things to keep an eye on, not yet actionable)
- {item} — {why}

### Noise (logged, intentionally ignored)
- {item} — {why it's not relevant}

---

**Rules of thumb**

- One theme per bullet block; never paste the whole changelog.
- Every claim links to a source the script actually saw.
- If nothing material changed, say so in one line and stop.
